{
  "rationale": "This is a first-iteration baseline with no race data yet, so I chose a conservative, symmetric design. Five line sensors spaced 12 mm apart span 48 mm, wider than the 25 mm tape, so the line stays visible through moderate bends. They sit 40 mm ahead of the axle so the robot reacts before it reaches the bend. Sensor weights of -2, -1, 0, 1, 2 give a signal that is roughly proportional to lateral offset, with the sign convention that positive steers left. A 12 mm footprint is a middle choice that resolves the tape edge without too much averaging. The controller uses base_speed 1.8, which is near full PWM and should give about 1.5 m/s or more, enough to finish within 3 s. kp 3.0 gives a strong but not saturating response (a signal of 1 produces about 1050 PWM of differential). A small ki of 0.05 removes steady bias from the motor mismatch, and a small kd of 0.1 damps oscillation without amplifying sensor noise. last_direction line-loss recovery keeps the robot turning toward where it last saw the tape. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with rms_error well under 0.05 m. The main risk is overshoot on the slalom at this speed, which I would check in steering_oscillation and max_error. Next measurements wanted: whether max_error approaches the off-track limit on the tightest bend, and the completion_time margin.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.024, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": -0.012, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.012, "y": 0.04},
      {"x": 0.024, "y": 0.04}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.8,
    "kp": 3.0,
    "ki": 0.05,
    "kd": 0.1,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "Symmetric five-sensor baseline with moderate gains (kp 3.0, base_speed 1.8) and last_direction line-loss recovery. No race data exists yet, so this is a conservative first build chosen from the contract ranges."
    }
  }
}
